### Corrects a cost already recorded, with optimistic locking.
### "version" is the one read from the shipment detail (shipment-detail.http).
### Sending the same request twice answers 409 the second time: the first one
### moved the version on, so the second is based on a value that is no longer current.
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/shipments/SHP-2026-0001/costs/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3200.00,
  "description": "Line haul, re-invoiced",
  "version": 0
}
